implementationPlan.description:
The chat store at state/chat.ts:28 already has ID-based dedup:
```typescript
if (thread.messages.some((m) => m.id === message.id)) {
    return state;
}
```
This is correct. The actual race is in useRunChat.ts where the same message arrives via:
1. `setMessages(runId, chatQuery.data.items)` (line 24) — API fetch
2. `addMessage(runId, message)` (line 59) — WebSocket event

The `setMessages` call replaces ALL messages, which could overwrite a WebSocket-added message. Fix: Change `setMessages` to merge instead of replace, using ID-based dedup:
```typescript
setMessages: (runId, messages) =>
    set((state) => {
        const threads = new Map(state.threads);
        const existing = threads.get(runId);
        const existingIds = new Set(existing?.messages.map(m => m.id) || []);
        const merged = [
            ...(existing?.messages || []),
            ...messages.filter(m => !existingIds.has(m.id)),
        ];
        threads.set(runId, { run_id: runId, messages: merged, status: "active" });
        return { threads };
    }),
```
